Fairtris 2 — the three places the game assumes it is on Windows.
Applies to a copy of the game's `source/` tree with `patch -p1`, from the
game's top directory. Never to the checkout itself.

Everything here is a compile-time guard. Nothing is removed, nothing is
rewritten, and a Windows or Linux build of the game reads exactly as it did
before: each guard's existing behaviour stays in the arm that already had it.

Fairtris.Clock.pp
    The frame limiter spins on an inline `pause` instruction while it waits
    for the next frame's tick. `pause` is x86. On aarch64 the assembler stops
    on the mnemonic, which reads as a broken assembler rather than as a
    wrong-architecture instruction. `yield` is the Arm instruction with the
    same meaning — a hint to the core that this thread is in a spin loop —
    so the arm added for CPUAARCH64 and CPUARM keeps the loop's behaviour.

Fairtris.Help.pp
    The help screen opens the project's web pages in the system browser,
    through the LCL unit LCLIntf. There is no browser on a bare-metal board,
    no LCL, and no Lazarus component library at all in this build. Under
    CIRCLESDL2 the unit is not used and OpenURL is not called; the screen
    still terminates the way it always did, which is what the rest of the
    game is waiting for.

Fairtris.Main.lpr
    The program links a Windows resource file, Fairtris.Main.res, which
    carries the executable's icon and version block. It is a PE resource,
    the file is not in the repository (Lazarus generates it), and no bare
    metal image has anywhere to put one. The directive is guarded to
    WINDOWS, where it already was in effect.
--- a/source/Fairtris.Clock.pp
+++ b/source/Fairtris.Clock.pp
@@ -231,9 +231,15 @@
   SDL_Delay(Round(SleepTime));
 
   while GetCounterValue() < FFrameTicksNext do
+  {$IF DEFINED(CPUAARCH64) OR DEFINED(CPUARM)}
   asm
+    yield
+  end;
+  {$ELSE}
+  asm
     pause
   end;
+  {$ENDIF}
 end;
 
 
--- a/source/Fairtris.Help.pp
+++ b/source/Fairtris.Help.pp
@@ -36,7 +36,9 @@
 implementation
 
 uses
+  {$IFNDEF CIRCLESDL2}
   LCLIntf,
+  {$ENDIF}
   Fairtris.Logic,
   Fairtris.Constants;
 
@@ -58,7 +60,9 @@
     SCENE_BSOD:        Address += 'BSoD';
   end;
 
+  {$IFNDEF CIRCLESDL2}
   OpenURL(Address);
+  {$ENDIF}
   Terminate();
 end;
 
--- a/source/Fairtris.Main.lpr
+++ b/source/Fairtris.Main.lpr
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@
 program Fairtris.Main;
 
 {$MODE OBJFPC}{$LONGSTRINGS ON}
-{$RESOURCE Fairtris.Main.res}
+{$IFDEF WINDOWS}{$RESOURCE Fairtris.Main.res}{$ENDIF}
 
 uses
   SDL2,
